      "problem": "At Joe's market, the unit price of tomatoes is $$5$ per pound. How many pounds of tomatoes can Geena buy for $$1?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the unit rate of $$5$ per pound (dollars per pound). To find how many pounds of tomatoes she can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in pounds per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n5\\,\\text{dollars per pound}\\,\\to \\,1÷5=0.2\\,\\text{pounds per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.2$ pounds per dollar. Therefore, Geena can buy $0.2$ pounds of tomatoes for $1$ dollar.",
